h nested tuplets. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bracket attribute is used to indicate the presence of a bracket. If unspecified, the results are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementation-dependent. The line-shape attribute is used to specify whether the bracket is straight or in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the older curved or slurred style. It is straight by default."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTuplet","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet","title":"MXLTuplet","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTuplet"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTuplet"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/s8CopyableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","title":"Swift.Copyable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/s8SendableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTuplet/Portion/Dot-swift.struct/font":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"font","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLFontV","text":"MXLFont","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltuplet\/portion\/dot-swift.struct\/font","abstract":[{"text":"The font attribute group gathers together attributes for determining the font within a credit or direction.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They are based on the text styles for Cascading Style Sheets. The font-family is a comma-separated list of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"font names.The font-style can be normal or italic. The font-size can be one of the CSS sizes or a numeric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point size. The font-weight can be normal or bold. The default is application-dependent, but is